## Analyzer, Linter & Type Hygiene (Mandatory)

### Mobile / Dart / Flutter

- After every change, run **`flutter analyze`** on touched code (or check IDE diagnostics) and **resolve all errors, warnings, and `info` lints** (`directives_ordering`, `unnecessary_import`, `deprecated_member_use`, etc.).
- Prefer **`dart fix --apply`** for auto-fixable lints before hand-editing.
- Treat deprecations as fix-now — never leave new analyzer issues for a follow-up.

### Web / TypeScript / JavaScript

- Run **`npm run lint`** and type checks (`tsc --noEmit` or project script) on touched work; resolve all errors and warnings before finishing.
- Prefer strict types over `any` or untyped casts.

### Other Stacks / Backends

- Run the repository's static analyzer, type checker, linter, and schema/migration validator before concluding work.

