## Async & Lifecycle Safety (Mandatory)

- **Always** check **`context.mounted`** / widget **`mounted`** (or component mount state / `AbortSignal`) after **`await`** before navigation, dialogs, bottom sheets, state updates, or toasts.
- Wrap async work in **`try/catch`**; **never** write empty **`catch (_) {}`** or silently swallow failures.
- Map/throw typed domain exceptions (**`AppException`** / **`Failure`**) in services and state controllers; log with structured logger (**`appLog`**) and report unexpected errors to crash reporting (`crashReporting.recordError`).
- Dismiss the keyboard before async submission and navigation:

```dart
SystemChannels.textInput.invokeMethod('TextInput.hide');
FocusScope.of(context).unfocus();
```

- Set **`autofocus: false`** on form fields unless the screen explicitly requires immediate focus (e.g., dedicated search or rename modal).
- Explicitly convert/cast **`dynamic`** / **`unknown`** values safely (e.g., `.toString()` or runtime validation) to avoid `argument_type_not_assignable` and runtime crashes.

---

## Colors API (Flutter Widgets)

- **Never** use **`withOpacity()`**.
- **Always** use **`withValues(alpha: …)`** on a semantic **`context.*`** color — e.g., `context.textPrimary.withValues(alpha: 0.5)`.

---

## Comments (see also `english-comments-only.mdc`)

- Keep comments **minimal and purposeful**. Remove redundant or stale comments in areas you edit.
- All developer comments remain **English only**.

---

## Terminal (Windows & Cross-Platform)

- **Never** chain commands with **`&&`** in Windows PowerShell or CMD — use **`;`**.
- Example: `cd C:\path\to\project; flutter analyze`
- Use **`&&`** only in bash / POSIX shells.

---

## General Habits

- Flutter: use **`const`** constructors wherever possible; use **`ListView.builder`** / **`GridView.builder`** (or virtualized lists on web) for long collections.
- Keep imports cleanly ordered: core SDK → third-party packages → project imports.
- Prefer **`final class`** + injected/top-level instance over static-only utility classes.
- Keep **one empty line at EOF** when the repository follows that convention.
- Design UI, layout, and caches for both **mobile and tablet** viewports (and desktop where applicable) — never expand frozen legacy web targets inside mobile codebases.

---

## Performance & Lazy Controller Initialization (Mandatory)

- **Lazy platform-channel & heavy controllers:** Never instantiate heavy platform-channel or worker controllers (e.g., `AudioPlayer`, camera/recorder/video controllers, heavy Web Worker pools, database handles) eagerly in field initializers; initialize them lazily on first use so widget/component construction stays lightweight, fast, and unit-testable.
- **Viewport list build purity:** Never spawn uncached async decrypt or network/DB futures inside list-item `build()` / render loops on every frame; always check synchronous in-memory caches first (`decryptTextCache`, `expressionCache`, `peekCachedKeysSync`, etc.) and assign stable keys (`ValueKey` in Flutter, stable `key` in React) to message, feed, and list items.
